Assume `outputs/r_validation/index.json` is `{"topics":[]}` and the review file is `A_REVIEW.html`.

- SELECTOR KEYED TO A FORM THE CORPUS MAY NOT USE: line 46. Input: `'NCT00000001_a': { tE:null,tN:10,cE:1,cN:10 } 'NCT00000002_b': { tE:null,tN:10,cE:1,cN:10 }`. Consequence: line 46 reports `n_ncts=0` even though line 11 will iterate both suffixed NCT blocks, so a multi-NCT review can be labeled `K_LE_1_LEGITIMATELY_UNPOOLABLE`.

- MERGED-CELL / COUNT UNIT ERROR: line 60. Input: `'NCT00000001': { tE:1,tN:10,cE:1,cN:10 } 'NCT00000001': { tE:2,tN:10,cE:2,cN:10 }`. Consequence: one unique trial becomes `binary_pool_eligible=2`, so line 78 can call a single-NCT review pool-eligible.

- SELECTOR KEYED TO WRONG FIELD FORM: lines 13-16. Input: `'NCT00000001': { "tE":1, "tN":10, "cE":1, "cN":10 } 'NCT00000002': { "tE":2, "tN":10, "cE":2, "cN":10 }`. Consequence: valid binary data with quoted JSON keys is missed and classified as atypical instead of eligible.

- SELECTOR/PARSER KEYED TO SINGLE-QUOTE STRINGS ONLY: lines 33-39. Input: `'NCT00000001': { note: "}", tE:1,tN:10,cE:1,cN:10 } 'NCT00000002': { note: "}", tE:1,tN:10,cE:1,cN:10 }`. Consequence: `find_balanced` treats `}` inside a double-quoted string as structural, truncating the block before the eligible data.

- ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT: line 23. Direct input: `to_int(0)`. Consequence: returns `None`, so any numeric zero passed by a caller is treated as absent; COULD NOT DETERMINE whether any external caller passes numeric values.

